Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 23:15:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] pdfium: admit AROS to the portable font backend

Pair the source-level platform guard with the GN selection that already reuses PDFium's folder-font implementation on AROS.

AI_PHASE: chromium-shared-cef

AI_STATUS: compile-failure-corrected-under-validation

AI_VALIDATION: prior rebuild reached fx_linux_impl.cpp and failed only its wrong-platform guard

AI_ASSUMPTION: BUILDFLAG(IS_AROS) is the exact platform discriminator supplied by Chromium build_config

AI_LIMITATIONS: archive rebuild, native link, and PDF rendering remain pending

AI_EVIDENCE: chromium-aros/src/out/aros-cef-bootstrap/test-artifacts/-cef-exact-44-fix-20260725/04-archive-rebuild-after-protobuf-localize.log

AI_DECISION_CHAIN:
---
 core/fxge/linux/fx_linux_impl.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/fxge/linux/fx_linux_impl.cpp b/core/fxge/linux/fx_linux_impl.cpp
index 031da7e..11e4c34 100644
--- a/core/fxge/linux/fx_linux_impl.cpp
+++ b/core/fxge/linux/fx_linux_impl.cpp
@@ -17,7 +17,8 @@
 #include "core/fxge/fx_font.h"
 #include "core/fxge/systemfontinfo_iface.h"
 
-#if !BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) && !BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS) && !defined(OS_ASMJS)
+#if !BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) && !BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS) && \
+    !BUILDFLAG(IS_AROS) && !defined(OS_ASMJS)
 #error "Included on the wrong platform"
 #endif
 
